Z||000005||Jimmy||06-23-2001||05:42 AM||||I also saw the "fast and the furious" today.  It was very OK.  I don't want to spoil it for anyone who hasn't seen it but its one of those "undercover cop things" that gets done over and over again.  I do think NOS paid up some big money so that their products or name was mentioned/shown every five minutes!  Overall the car stuff was fun!  Better than Gone in 60 Seconds(200) which I thought had crummy footage of cars.  Hmmmm.... I've been looking at NOS kits for my V8 on the internet all night, movie must have served its purpose.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jimmy||06-23-2001||05:44 AM||||Oh, and the muscle car in the movie was a Charger not a GTO.  Not really what year however.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||06-23-2001||10:37 AM||||I saw it yesterday too. You hear mention on turbo's & superchargers, but the movie highlights NOS a hell of alot. EVERY car has NOS, except the Charger. Some cars did look good, while others had "too much" rice to them, to the point of being ridiculous. Check out <A HREF="http://www.beaterz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.beaterz.com</A>   to see some "overcooked rice".<P>I expect NOS sales will skyrocket this summer, as every Honda CRX/Civic owner will be installing NOS and a fart-can exhaust expecting to become a 10sec race car.  I doubt many will spend the other thousands of dollars to make the engine stronger, so expect to see many Hondas with blown engines being towed off the street.<P>The movie is SOOO realistic.  Like, ya, the slammed cars can do 160mph on city streets!! You can race 4 abreast, and there's NO traffic and NO cops in L.A. Every kid with a better than minimum -wage job has spent US$40,000 on his US$20,000 Honda.  The one guy has an S2000 with "probably $100,000 under the hood"!!  Like all 20 year-olds are THAT rich!!<P>Entertaining movie though.  I enjoyed it, probably more than Gone in 60 Seconds...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 06-23-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||Tweek||06-23-2001||11:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>Oh, and the muscle car in the movie was a Charger not a GTO.  Not really what year however.<P>Jim</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Doh!  My bad.||||reg||1
Z||000009||c m west||06-23-2001||12:13 PM||||You can race 4 abreast, and there's NO traffic and NO cops in L.A. - this is true, especially at 3 in the morning on Roxford and Tampa where it is really done<P>Every kid with a better than minimum -wage job has spent US$40,000 on his US$20,000 - there called sponserships, either through stereo companies or through some less "legal" means. <P>The one guy has an S2000 with "probably $100,000 under the hood"!! Like all 20 year-olds are THAT rich!! Im sure the character's mommy and daddy had some participation in it, just as they do in real life<P>I grew up with street racing here in L.A. and the movie wasnt that far off. The only thing I found a stretch was the big rig hi-jacking, though it may give some kids even better ideas for funds to add to the money hungry cars<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||06-24-2001||05:26 AM||||The one guy has an S2000 with "probably $100,000 under the hood"!! Like all 20 year-olds are THAT rich!!<BR>I was half asleep through the movie [I thought it sucked by the way] and still noticed that the kid in the "Honda 2000" as they kept calling it, was forshadowed as a spoiled rich kid in the beginning of the movie.<P>Besides a nitrous backfire, how would a 140 shot of NOS attempt to "crack the welds on the intake" Yeah it could freeze the intake and it could crack thawing out, but they made 140 seem like a magic number and if something happened to break the intake with that much nitrous, the intake would be the last thing I would be worrying about. ||||reg||1
