Z||000013||Neal||06-24-2001||08:34 PM||||well the eclipse he was driving is supposed to be 10 sec in the quarter, which would make him WAY faster than the ferarri, but in hollywood style the 10 sec car is neck and neck with a 12-13 sec car...<P>And in a drag dont you want to get on the n2o ASAP?<BR>Also for 10 sec out of an import would you not need a much bigger shot than 140.  And shouldnt the interiors have been totally striped for weight savings...<P>So many things bothered me, but i keep telling myself its hollywood.||||reg||1
Z||000014||kslish||06-24-2001||10:19 PM||||They were driving a Toyota Supra Turbo when they took on the Ferrari (which is a fair fight).  I don't think that the Eclipse that the lead character was driving at the beginning of the movie was anywhere near a 10 second car.  <P>The Supra is simply in a different league compared to the other cars in the movie.  It's equivalents would be Acura NSX's, Vette's, and so on.<P>Ken S.   ||||reg||1
Z||000015||JSocha||06-25-2001||09:15 AM||||I thought the movie was a heck of a lot better then DRIVEN, had a plot and the action and tension was all there.  Sure beats watching the Little Mermaid!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Some of the eye candy was good, especially the shower scene at Car Wars.<P>Wife didn't like it to much.  But she did like the colors of the cars.<P>I thought the Wheelie the Charger did at the end of the movie was awsum!<P><B>EDIT:</B>  Did anybody realize something in that movie as did I.  Hardly anybody (well, actually nobody for that matter) was ever wearing their seatbelts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  RECARO seats with dual sholder straps and yet every scene, no seatbelts.<P>Wife noticed that too!<BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
